#
# Counter-example for math:MultiparameterFunctionalDependenceConstraint: a
# math:MultiparameterFiltration with TWO stages whose math:multiIndex coordinates are
# functionally dependent via an AFFINE map (t, 2t) — NOT the literal diagonal (t, t)
# math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltrationConstraint alone would catch. Stage 1 sits at (1, 2)
# and stage 2 at (2, 4): the second coordinate is always exactly twice the first, so no
# pair of stages ever varies one coordinate while holding the other fixed — at every
# pair BOTH coordinates differ together. The coordinate-independence witness the
# general constraint requires (two stages sharing one math:componentValue node while
# differing at the other) therefore cannot exist, so
# math:MultiparameterFunctionalDependenceConstraint fires — shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent
# (math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltration). ISOLATION: the filtration IS complete for its
# frame (math:filtrationIndexPoset and two math:hasFiltrationStage cells present), so
# math:IncompleteMultiparameterFiltration stays silent; a math:multiIndex IS present on
# both stages, so math:CollapsedMultiparameterFiltration cannot fire; neither stage's
# OWN multi-index repeats a componentValue node across its two positions, so the
# single-stage math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltrationConstraint stays silent too — isolating
# this cross-stage functional-dependence detection specifically. So EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:DiagonalDegenerateFiltration, math:MultiparameterFunctionalDependenceConstraint
# (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecMultiparameterAffineDegenerate).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/affine/> .

ex:affine a math:MultiparameterFiltration ;
    math:filtrationIndexPoset ex:grid ;
    math:hasFiltrationStage ex:stage1 , ex:stage2 .

ex:grid a math:MathematicalObject .

# Stage 1 at (1, 2).
ex:stage1 a math:FiltrationStage ; math:multiIndex ex:index1 .
ex:index1 a math:Vector ; math:hasComponent ex:s1c0 , ex:s1c1 .
ex:s1c0 a math:VectorComponent ; math:atIndex 0 ; math:componentValue ex:one .
ex:s1c1 a math:VectorComponent ; math:atIndex 1 ; math:componentValue ex:two .

# Stage 2 at (2, 4) — the second coordinate is always exactly TWICE the first, an
# affine (t, 2t) dependence, not the literal diagonal.
ex:stage2 a math:FiltrationStage ; math:multiIndex ex:index2 .
ex:index2 a math:Vector ; math:hasComponent ex:s2c0 , ex:s2c1 .
ex:s2c0 a math:VectorComponent ; math:atIndex 0 ; math:componentValue ex:two .
ex:s2c1 a math:VectorComponent ; math:atIndex 1 ; math:componentValue ex:four .

ex:one  a math:RationalValue ; math:numerator 1 ; math:denominator 1 ; math:isExact true .
ex:two  a math:RationalValue ; math:numerator 2 ; math:denominator 1 ; math:isExact true .
ex:four a math:RationalValue ; math:numerator 4 ; math:denominator 1 ; math:isExact true .
